It would appear so, yes. But I wouldn't exactly call that evidence. 
After all, it might just do that because that is the bottom right, and 
it don't know better. Unless I remember wrong, RT-11 don't keep 
information around as for how many lines a terminal have, so unless the 
program itself tries to figure it out, 24 lines would be the safe 
assumption.

In RSX, the number of lines of a terminal is kept by the OS, and 
programs can read it out, and adapt, if they want to.
However, EDT, which is the only DEC screen editor, does not handle more 
than 24 lines, even if your terminal says it have more. EDT however, do 
handle both 80 and 132 columns. But not (as far as I know) any other widths.

