Correct. You can, as a system administrator, create a common region 
which happens to be the I7O page, and then user programs could map that 
in, with the normal system calls, into their address space. But the 
sysadm who do this, is asking for his system to crash.

By the way, all my answers are only valid for mapped RSX systems. 
Unmapped systems runs without any MMU, and then the I/O page is 
accessible (obviously), so that is an entirely different ballgame.

> As for running with the PSW set to 14xxxx, I am fairly confident that
