I had half a dozen RL02 drives with racks and many
media.  Also 2 * 9 track tape drives and 2 * LA120.
I refuse to use ebay and being in Toronto there was
absolutely on interest in pickup.

I finally managed last year to find a good home.

Since I am a software addict, it should not have
bothered me to see them disposed of,  But I
felt that they should not go to the dumpster.

Of course, I also see a total lack of interest in
RT-11 bug fixes and enhancements.  So I guess
that the software will also be eventually tossed.

Meanwhile, there is a new NuPDQ-1000 Qbus
board.  It is really an emulator using an Intel chip,
but I hear it runs about 100 times a PDP-11/93.
I hear that the sales are thus far are completely for
RSX-11.

