Ah! Cool. Well, an 11/74 would not need a PCL-11. Since memory is 
shared, all data is always available to all CPUs without any transfers 
at all. The only thing needed is a way to interrupt one CPU from 
another, and that is provided by the IIST. The IIST is also responsible 
for booting CPUs, and it also have the sanity timer, so that the system 
can detect if everything hangs.

You could use a PCL-11 as a way to network up to 16 11/74 systems. But I 
think that an ethernet interface would be better at this point. :-)

	Johnny



