Ethernet would indeed have had some advantages, if it (and the
required DECnet software) had been around at the time. but (a) the
PCL11 was a late 70s thing whereas the Digital/Intel/Xerox Ethernet
spec was published in 1980 and DECnet Phase IV with Ethernet support
was a mid 1980s thing iirc (b) the PCL11 was largely DMA-driven which
in the days of the DEUNA and such would probably have been of
interest.

I never actually used a PCL11 for real so if I happen to be defending
a piece of crock, I do apologise. The concept sounded nice though.


