On Wed, 6 Jul 2011 at 01:13 +0200, Johnny Billquist wrote:

> Hmm, and before EDT was shipped...? That gotta move us back to 
> atleast RSX-11M V2 I would suspect. That's very long ago. Did KED 
> exist back then?

KED predated EDT and was largely replaced by EDT (IE, hardly anybody 
stuck with KED after being introduced to EDT). EDT was not distributed 
until RSX-11M V4.x.  I think I first used it in V4.2 about 1982.  I 
think it was available in the previous version (V4.1?), but I never 
used that version.  I am certain it was not available with V3.2. But 
there was a time with V3.2 that people were raving about KED. I tried 
KED, but was not amazed enough to switch.  I don't recall how we got 
it.  I think it was undocumented and unsupported.  It either magically 
appeared during SYSGEN, or was passed around at DECUS lug meetings.

Maybe we should check the Multi-taskers from 1979 and 1980.

DEC folk of the M 3.2 era used KED all the time.  In our shop we 
picked up a version of UNIX ed (ued) ported to M and tricked up to 
display a window into the file you were editing.


