On Wed, 6 Jul 2011 10:09:01 -0600, Rob Brown <mylastname@gmcl.com>
wrote:

>I am certain it was not available with V3.2. But 
>there was a time with V3.2 that people were raving about KED. I tried 
>KED, but was not amazed enough to switch.  I don't recall how we got 
>it.  I think it was undocumented and unsupported.  It either magically 
>appeared during SYSGEN, or was passed around at DECUS lug meetings.

That rings a bell with me--but it's just a vague, distant memory.

A lot of RT-11 development took place on an 11/70-based RSTS system
(actually one of the 11/74's IIRC), but I guess KED was used in the
RSTS RT-11 environment. Some later development may have taken place
under RSX using RTEM, but that was much later than the period under
discussion.

Getting a decent editor was a problem in the period (we did our own).
The RT-11 kit included a deleted copy of TECO for many years. The
first act of receiving a new kit was to undelete TECO.SAV. So an
internal port to RSX would not be unreasonable. However, one would
expect the conditionals to remain in the source code.

I'm trying to remember with KED.SAV and K52.SAV arrived on the RT-11
kit (I never used it at the time--way too slow). It was probably
around the time of the transition to the VT100 series.

Ian

