A little further digging and the first mention I find of RT-11 KED was
in the March 1979 RT-11 V3b release notes where it is listed as a
component of the optional software package FMS-11 (FORMS-11). So I
it's possible that KED was initially developed as a screen editor for
the FORMS-11 package.

http://www.bitsavers.org/pdf/dec/pdp11/rt11/v3b_Mar79
AA-5285D-TC-RT11v3bDocDir.pdf

By January 1980 KED was part of the regular RT-11 V4.0 distribution.

http://www.bitsavers.org/pdf/dec/pdp11/rt11/v4.0_Mar80/1a/
AA-5285E-TC_RT-11_V4.0_Documentation_Directory_Jan80.pdf

The software manual for RSX FMS-11 was first printed in January 1980.
The package includes a description of "FED", a dedicated forms editor
which has KED-like keyboard operation.

http://www.archive.org/stream/fms11_rsx_v10_software_reference_manual#page/n19/mode/2up

So a picture emerges where RSX had a dedicated forms editor where
RT-11 had a more general-purpose editor. It's possible that the RSX
editor required more space or made use of RSX-specific features. 

The RSX-11M(plus) stand-alone KED release notes noted earlier are
dated March 1980.





Ian


