Spent quite a few years programming macro under rt11, but very little under
rsx. One thing I do remember was the task monitor, a bit like top
or prstat on unix / solaris, but to a terminal using direct cursor
addressing. Remember sitting around waiting around at the screen for it
to do it's shuffler run, which (as you know, but others may not) recovered
all the free blocks in memory by shuffling all the tasks down. An 
interesting
technique that i've not seen used on any other os, but efficient enough that
it could be usefull for embedded work...

Regards,

Chris


